# No em dashes in copy or design

Do not use em dashes (`—`) or en dashes (`–`) anywhere in user-facing content for this project.

## Applies to

- Page titles and meta descriptions
- Headlines, eyebrows, body copy, CTAs, labels, and microcopy
- Footer, nav, forms, legal pages, and service pages
- Error messages and button text shown to users

## Use instead

- Comma: `Talk to an engineer, not a sales bot.`
- Period: `We deploy tools. We operate them.`
- Colon for lists: `Layered defense: EDR, firewalls, SIEM`
- Middle dot for pairs/locations: `San Diego · Las Vegas`
- Parentheses when needed: `Message (optional)`

## Exceptions

- Code comments and internal developer notes are fine to keep as-is
- Hyphen-minus `-` in code, class names, URLs, and compound words (e.g. `24/7`, `AI-powered`) is allowed

When editing existing copy, replace any remaining em/en dashes with the alternatives above.
